<title>SWITZERLAND: Swiss newspaper ad pages drop 6.4 pct in January.</title>
<headline>Swiss newspaper ad pages drop 6.4 pct in January.</headline>
<dateline>ZURICH 1997-02-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Advertising pages in Swiss newspapers fell 6.4 percent in January compared with a year earlier, according to figures compiled by the WEMF media tracking agency: (pct change in pages vs year-ago) Jan</p>
<p> Daily/weekly newspapers		  - 6.4</p>
<p> Commercial ads			     - 2.3</p>
<p>    Employment ads			 - 28.1</p>
<p> Free newspapers			    + 3.2</p>
<p>    Commercial ads			  + 7.0</p>
<p>    Employment ads			 - 37.1</p>
<p> Magazines				    + 9.9</p>
<p>    Multicolour ads			+ 18.4</p>
<p>    Black and white ads		   - 4.3</p>
<p> Specialised publications		 + 5.5</p>
<p>    Multicolour ads			+ 25.5</p>
<p>    Black and white ads		   - 0.1</p>
<p>The Association of Swiss Advertising Companies (VSW) said the figures tended to overstate the drop. It said a more useful comparison would use the number of pages per editions appearing, which helped reflect an industry consolidation last year. This system showed a drop of 2.7 percent among newspapers but reduced the growth in magazine ad pages to 1.6 percent.</p>
<p>-- Zurich newsroom +41 1 631 7340</p>
</text>
